# Contributing to {{.AppTitle}} SDK

## Prerequisites

- Smithy CLI
- Go 1.22+
- Node.js 20+
- Ruby 3.2+
- Make

## Development Workflow

1. Fork and clone the repository
2. Create a feature branch: `git checkout -b my-feature`
3. Make changes following the patterns in AGENTS.md
4. Run checks: `make check`
5. Commit and push
6. Open a pull request

## Adding a New API Operation

1. Add the operation to the Smithy spec in `spec/model/`
2. Run `make smithy-build` to regenerate OpenAPI
3. Regenerate the service layer. `make generate-services` covers every language this SDK
   ships; to do one at a time use `make go-generate-services`,
   `make ts-generate-services`, `make rb-generate-services`,
   `make kt-generate-services`, or `make swift-generate`.
4. Add unit tests
5. Add conformance tests if the operation has behavioral requirements
6. Run `make check`

## Release Process

Releases are managed via `make release VERSION=x.y.z`. See MAKEFILE-CONVENTION.md
in basecamp/sdk for the target vocabulary and release architecture.
